WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.672
We will begin with a very small table so the structure is easy to see.

00:00:04.672 --> 00:00:11.802
The example imports Pandas and creates an orders DataFrame from several dictionary records.

00:00:11.802 --> 00:00:19.492
Each dictionary represents one order, and the dictionary keys become column names such as order I D, channel,

00:00:19.492 --> 00:00:20.392
and amount.

00:00:20.392 --> 00:00:29.322
Small manually created tables are useful for learning because we already know what the correct data should look like.

00:00:29.322 --> 00:00:36.732
They are also useful in professional work when you want to test a calculation or a cleaning rule before applying it to a

00:00:36.732 --> 00:00:38.902
much larger dataset.

00:00:38.902 --> 00:00:46.343
When you run the code, look at how Pandas automatically organizes the records into rows and labeled columns.
